* #variable= 5 #constraint= 8
* An equivalence stands for the two directions of the same constraint, in the order in which they
* would be written out.
z1 <==> +1 x1 +2 x2 >= 2 ;
z2 <==> 1 x1 1 x2 <= 1 ;
* The literal may be negated, and the constraint is normalized before it is reified.
~z3 <==> 3 x1 2 ~x1 >= 3 ;
* A trivially satisfied constraint is implied by anything, and implies the literal; a contradicting
* constraint implies anything, and is implied by nothing.
z4 <==> 1 x1 >= 0 ;
z5 <==> 1 x1 >= 5 ;
